  "final_answer": "## BRK.B support and resistance, past year (Sep 29 2025 to Sep 25 2026)\n\n**Bottom line:** BRK.B has moved sideways all year. It closed Friday (Sep 25) at **$505.48**, about 1% above where it was a year ago. The 52-week range is **$464.01 (Apr 16) to $537.74 (Aug 10)**, so price sits about 56% of the way up. The nearest levels are support at about $500 and resistance at about $510\u2013513. Don't use four of the six levels the support/resistance tool returned; they aren't real (explained below).\n\n### Levels from the daily price history (250 sessions)\n\n**Resistance (above $505.48)**\n| Zone | What happened there |\n|---|---|\n| **$510\u2013513** | Nearest ceiling. Four of the last six sessions topped out here (512.07, 510.50, 511.28, 510.00). Rallies also stalled here on Nov 13\u201326 2025 (up to 514.26), Feb 4 (512.13), Jul 7 (512.58) and Jul 28\u201329 (513.44). |\n| **$516\u2013518** | Two tops in Nov 2025 (516.55, 516.85), plus Aug 4 (517.77) and Sep 15 (516.87). |\n| **$520\u2013525** | Aug 3 (520.67), Aug 6 (525.44) and the Sep 16 swing high (523.74). |\n| **$530\u2013538** | The 52-week high: 537.74 on Aug 10, then 530.30 on Aug 11. Price fell to $510 within two sessions, so sellers turned it back hard. |\n\n**Support (below $505.48)**\n| Zone | What happened there |\n|---|---|\n| **$499\u2013502** | Nearest floor. Lows of 500.70 (Sep 8), 501.21, 501.27, 501.41 and 501.98 this month, and 499.22 on Aug 27. |\n| **$495\u2013496.5** | The Aug 21 swing low (495.68) and Aug 20 (496.48). The same level held in Nov 2025 (495.13, 495.55) and Feb 2026 (495.50, 495.68). |\n| **$486\u2013490** | The floor of the June\u2013July range (485.77, 486.06, 486.17, 486.50), plus lows from Oct and Dec 2025 (487.82, 488.92). |\n| **$471\u2013475** | Lows from Oct\u2013Nov 2025 (473.15, 473.72), Jan 28 (471.91), Mar 3 (472.52) and May 29 (472.27). |\n| **$464\u2013468** | The main base for the year. It was tested about eight times between late Mar and early Jun: 464.01 (the 52-week low), 464.34, 464.62, 465.64, 465.79, 467.21, 467.96 and 468.21. |\n\n**Near-term setup:** Since Aug 21, price has traded between about $496 and $524. Right now it is stuck between $500 and $513. A daily close above $513 would open the way to $517 and then $524. A close below $499 would likely retest $495\u2013496, and below that $486\u2013490.\n\n### Four of the tool's six levels are made up\n`technical_get_support_resistance` returned support **[454.93, 480.21, 495.68]** and resistance **[523.74, 530.75, 556.03]**. When I checked them against the price history:\n- **495.68** (Aug 21 low) and **523.74** (Sep 16 high) are real prices from the chart.\n- The other four are just the last close ($505.48) times fixed percentages. None of them came from the price history:\n  - 505.48 \u00d7 0.90 = 454.93\n  - 505.48 \u00d7 0.95 = 480.21\n  - 505.48 \u00d7 1.05 = 530.75\n  - 505.48 \u00d7 1.10 = 556.03\n- 454.93 is below the 52-week low (464.01) and 556.03 is above the 52-week high (537.74), so price never traded at either level this year.\n- The `days` setting had no effect: `days=365` and `days=90` gave exactly the same output. The tool never showed the 52-week high or low, which suggests it only looks at recent weeks whatever you ask for.\n\nI didn't read the tool's source code, so the \u00b15% and \u00b110% padding is inferred from the numbers. It is exact to the cent on all four values. This looks like a defect worth checking in the support/resistance code: the padded levels come back in the same list as the real ones, with nothing to tell them apart, and `days` is ignored.\n\n**Data notes:** the quote timestamp is Sunday Sep 27, so $505.48 is Friday's close (up $0.30 from Thursday's $505.18). The ticker `BRK.B` worked as written for all calls. No files were created.",
